OL,4,C
OL,5,CDUBLINFEvelyn Glenholmes
OL,6,F freed a second time...........103B203
OL,8,CNORTHERN IRELANDFHurd warns
OL,9, FUnionists over agreement......104B204
OL,10,F
OL,11,CWAPPINGF8,000 marchers converge
OL,12,F on print works................114B214
OL,14,CNUCLEAR TESTSFUS goes ahead....105B205
OL,15,F Owen urges test ban...........106B206
OL,16,F
OL,17,CPETROLFMotorists queue at
OL,18,F "no rise" garages.............108B208
OL,19,F
OL,20,CCRICKETFThird Test latest......141
OL,22,T]F This Ceefax page is fromC22-03-86
OL,23,T]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49604
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Evelyn Glenholmes, the Belfast woman
OL,6, named as an IRA murder suspect by
OL,7, Scotland Yard, has twice been freed by
OL,8, a Dublin court.
OL,10,FEarlier today the court rejected an
OL,11,Fapplication for her extradition to
OL,12,FBritain and she was released.
OL,14,FAfter a car chase through Dublin and a
OL,15,Ftussle with her supporters, she was
OL,16,Fre-arrested on a provisional warrant
OL,17,Fobtained by the Irish police.
OL,19,FBut on her second appearance in court
OL,20,Fa police application to remand her in
OL,21,Fcustody until the arrival of new
OL,22,Fextradition documents from Britain
OL,23,Fwas refused.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Home Secretary has warned Unionist
OL,6, leaders that their opposition to the
OL,7, Anglo-Irish agreement is jeopardising
OL,8, the progress made in Northern Ireland.
OL,10,FMr Douglas Hurd said at a meeting in
OL,11,FSwindon that the people of Northern
OL,12,FIreland had painstakingly dragged the
OL,13,Fprovince back from the edge of disaster
OL,15,FThese achievements were now at risk for
OL,16,Fthe sake of old slogans and ancient
OL,17,Fsuspicions.
OL,19,FThe best hope for Northern Ireland is
OL,20,Fwith "consultation and cooperation
OL,21,Frather than confrontation", he said.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, About 8,000 newspaper, print and
OL,6, distribution workers have marched to
OL,7, the News International print works in
OL,8, east London.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThey have joined about 200 pickets
OL,11,Foutside the main entrance.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe organisers appear to have planned
OL,14,Fa peaceful march past the plant.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FBut the demonstrators decided to halt
OL,17,Foutside the main gate, completely
OL,18,Fblocking the road and preventing
OL,19,Fnewspaper lorries from coming out.
OL,20,F
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The United States has carried out its
OL,6, first nuclear weapons test this year
OL,7, at a desert site in Nevada.
OL,9,FA device was detonated 2,000ft beneath
OL,10,Fthe desert - in spite of a Soviet offer
OL,11,Fof a joint test ban.
OL,13,FEarlier this month Moscow said that it
OL,14,Fwould continue its nine-month-old test
OL,15,Fmoratorium past the March 31 expiry
OL,16,Fdate.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FNews of the test prompted an immediate
OL,19,Foutcry in Congress where President
OL,20,FReagan has been under pressure to
OL,21,Fresume negotiations with Moscow for a
OL,22,Fcomprehensive test ban treaty.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 22-03-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, SDP leader Dr David Owen has called on
OL,6, Britain to stop the testing of nuclear
OL,7, weapons.
OL,9,FIn an interview with the Press
OL,10,FAssociation he said today's test in
OL,11,FNevadaFshould be the last.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FHe also urged that Britain should
OL,14,Fresume talks with the United States and
OL,15,Fthe Soviet Union over achieving a
OL,16,Fcomprehensive nuclear test ban.
OL,18,FDr Owen condemned Conservative MPs'
OL,19,Facceptance of British nuclear testing,
OL,20,Faccusing Mrs Thatcher of acting as
OL,21,F"Little Miss Echo" to President Reagan.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774186984
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Queues formed at garages selling "no
OL,6, rise" petrol today, while elsewhere
OL,7, price increases of between 2p and
OL,8, 7.5p were reported after the budget.
OL,10,FWhere the full budget increase has been
OL,11,Fpassed on, the cost of a gallon of
OL,12,Fpetrol has risen to #1.85.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FBut the AA reported prices as low as
OL,15,F#1.58 a gallon in Cardiff and #1.59
OL,16,Fat a garage in south-east England.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FConfusion over exactly how much of the
OL,19,Fbudget increase drivers would have to
OL,20,Fpay follows criticism of the big oil
OL,21,Fcompanies by Mrs Thatcher.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
